WHY THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Nothing in it is secret. It is the frontend
of coderoast.fr: the shipped JavaScript bundle is already served to every
visitor, and the backend surface it talks to (routes, entitlement keys and
quota limits) is returned by the public API to unauthenticated callers by
design. Publishing the source therefore discloses nothing the running site
does not, while keeping the repository's CI free and its history open to
inspection. The CodeRoast moat — the validation harness, the production
scenario library, and the detection engine — is not in this repository.

Third-party dependencies keep their own licences; see package.json and the
NOTICE of each dependency.

For any use beyond reading: contact emmanuel.prunet@coderoast.fr
